---
import ClosingCTA from "../../components/ClosingCTA.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
import Video from "../../components/Video.astro";
import { guide } from "../../data/site";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	description="See 0xlillith’s SELENE rover, modeled through SolidCraft MCP, with a timeline replay and source model repository."
	title="SELENE · A rover modeled through SolidCraft MCP"
>
	<section class="page-intro container">
		<p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/showcase/">Showcase</a> / SELENE</p>
		<p class="eyebrow">AGENT WORKFLOW / 0XLILLITH</p>
		<h1>SELENE rover.</h1>
		<p class="lead">
			A scientific rover built through SolidCraft’s MCP server. An editable
			assembly, from the chassis and wheels to the solar wings and camera
			turret.
		</p>
	</section>
	<div class="container full-demo"><Video model="rover" /></div>
	<div class="container model-details">
		<div>
			<h2>3,323 timeline steps.</h2>
			<p>
				The upstream project presents SELENE as a rover created by 0xlillith
				through SolidCraft MCP, with 3,323 editable timeline steps. Its
				recording replays that timeline at 2× speed.
			</p>
			<p>
				The replay shows the assembly taking shape. It is a timeline recording,
				not a recording of the agent conversation or a claim that the full
				modeling process took a minute.
			</p>
			<h2 style="margin-top:40px">Open the source model.</h2>
			<p>
				The creator’s repository contains the editable model and its own notes.
				Download a supported design file there, open it in SolidCraft, and
				inspect its timeline. Check the repository’s build and licensing
				information before reusing it.
			</p>
			<div class="actions">
				<a
					class="button primary"
					href="https://github.com/0xlillith/solidcraft-rover"
				>
					Model & source repository<Icon name="external" size={18} />
				</a>
				<a class="text-link" href="/mcp/">
					MCP setup and tools<Icon size={18} />
				</a>
			</div>
			<div class="notice">
				SELENE is a conceptual model. The recording does not establish physical
				feasibility, manufacturing readiness, or independently verified
				engineering performance.
			</div>
		</div>
		<aside>
			<dl>
				<dt>Model creator</dt>
				<dd><a href="https://github.com/0xlillith">0xlillith</a></dd>
				<dt>Recording</dt>
				<dd>SolidCraft contributors</dd>
				<dt>Playback</dt>
				<dd>2× timeline replay</dd>
				<dt>Recording license</dt>
				<dd>MIT OR Apache-2.0, per upstream attribution</dd>
				<dt>Model lettering</dt>
				<dd>Ubuntu Light outlines; see creator’s repository notices.</dd>
				<dt>Recorded build</dt>
				<dd>
					SolidCraft 0.22.1 (a build of the main branch), replaying the
					creator’s Rover-recorded.solidcraft.
				</dd>
			</dl>
			<a class="text-link" href={guide("mcp")}>
				MCP setup guide<Icon name="external" size={18} />
			</a>
		</aside>
	</div>
	<ClosingCTA />
</BaseLayout>
